WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.240
TERRY RYAN: Today we're
talking about serverless

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.867
Spark, limitless data, baseball,
and enterprise learning.

00:00:05.867 --> 00:00:08.450
I'm Terry, and welcome to "This
Week in Cloud," where we serve

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.700
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.617
Earlier this year we
made serverless Spark

00:00:12.617 --> 00:00:14.450
generally available,
creating the industry's

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.677
first autoscaling
serverless Spark.

00:00:16.677 --> 00:00:18.260
And now we're taking
it a step further

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:19.910
and making serverless
Spark even more

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.550
powerful by enabling serverless
interactive development

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.800
through Jupyter Notebooks,
natively integrated

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.480
with Vertex AI Workbench.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.090
Now a data scientist will
not need to provision

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.500
any infrastructure in advance.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.960
They can just start
developing on demand.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.550
With the dramatic
growth in the amount

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.650
and types of data,
workloads, and users,

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.110
we are at a point where
traditional data architectures,

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.480
even when deployed in the
cloud, are unable to unlock

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.830
its full potential.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:45.530
As a result, the
data-to-value gap is growing.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.090
To address these
challenges, we're

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:48.950
unveiling several
data cloud innovations

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.290
that allow customers to
work with limitless data

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.630
across all workloads,
and extend access

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:56.900
to everyone, from BigLake
and Spanner change streams

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.120
to Vertex AI Workbench
and model registry.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.160
Check out the blog for more.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.260
Baseball and
statistics go way back.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:04.849
These days cloud
technology enables

00:01:04.849 --> 00:01:08.930
MLB to collect and analyze
25 million unique data points

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:12.443
from each of its 2,430
regular season games.

00:01:12.443 --> 00:01:14.360
From helping players
improve their performance

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.370
to bringing fans
closer to the action,

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:18.380
we'll walk you through
a few ways MLB is

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:21.188
hitting a grand slam with data.

00:01:21.188 --> 00:01:22.980
There are countless
reasons why enterprises

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.170
are moving to the cloud,
from reduced IT costs

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.910
to improved security
and efficiency.

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.910
But how will organizations
accelerate cloud adoption

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:32.230
within their organizations?

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:35.100
The answer is
comprehensive training.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.040
Google Cloud Skills Boost
combines award-winning learning

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.230
experiences with the
ability to earn credentials

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:43.230
to validate learning, which
can be managed and delivered

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:46.320
directly by Google Cloud with
enterprise-level features.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.360
Learn more about our
research-driven courses

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.017
and how you can get
started on the blog.

00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:53.100
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.630
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:56.910
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:59.350
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:02.420
We'll see you in the cloud.

